Usage:
  codebase-memory-mcp cli query_graph --flag value [--flag2 value2 ...]
  codebase-memory-mcp cli query_graph --args-file <path-to-json>
  echo '<json>' | codebase-memory-mcp cli query_graph
  codebase-memory-mcp cli query_graph '<raw-json-args>'

Flags:
  --query <string> [required]  Cypher query
  --project <string> [required]
  --graph <code|missed> [default: code]  code graph (default) or missed coverage-gap file tree.
  --max-rows <integer> [default: 200]  Visible rows (default 200; max 99998); 0 uses the legacy maximum. Evaluation is unchanged.
  --offset <integer> [default: 0]  Live compatibility paging; cannot be combined with cursor.
  --cursor <string>  Snapshot continuation; keep query/project/graph. Format, budget, and max_rows may change.
  --max-output-tokens <integer>  Sizing hint; hard ceiling is 4 UTF-8 bytes/token. Rows stay whole.
  --format <tree|json> [default: tree]  tree may use local @N+suffix prefix refs; json uses direct strings.
